fields.description:
How the product is sold, one of:
- `simple`: one variant, nothing to choose;
- `multiple`: variants, chosen by `options`;
- `digital`: a download;
- `bundle`: several products sold together, added with `cartBundleAdd`
  (never `cartLinesAdd`); `bundle` describes them.

Read at no cost for a list of products, unlike `bundle`, which loads
each bundle's products.

enumValues.description:
Added for the buyer: the platform puts the offered products into the cart at
the offer's price. After an add to cart `cartLinesAdd` has already done it;
the cart page's offer is added with `cartCrossSellApply`.

inputFields.description:
The answer. For a field offering options this is the chosen option's label;
for a checkbox, the value the merchant configured. Sending null leaves the
field unanswered.
